{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Scope decision + evidence.\n\nPR #125 bundles two bumps in dependabot's 'uv-lock' group:\n  * zizmor 1.28.0 -> 1.29.0  (LANDING here)\n  * mcp     1.29.0 -> 2.0.0  (EXCLUDED; deferred to 732b-51df-acf2-477b)\n\nThe mcp half is a straight re-proposal of what dependabot already asked for in PR #124\n(now CLOSED). Ticket 1dfd-063e-f341-48da investigated it and rejected it on evidence:\nmcp 2.0 removes mcp.server.fastmcp. Re-verified against this worktree's tree at\norigin/main c89a2ddcc4 — the v1 import paths are still present and unchanged:\n\n  src/rebar/mcp_server.py:570         from mcp.server.fastmcp import FastMCP\n  scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py:72     from mcp.server.fastmcp import FastMCP\n  src/rebar/mcp_server.py:512         from mcp.server.transport_security import TransportSecuritySettings\n  src/rebar/mcp_server.py:590         from mcp.server.auth.settings import AuthSettings\n  src/rebar/_mcp_auth.py:38           from mcp.server.auth.provider import AccessToken\n  src/rebar/_mcp_models.py:291        from mcp.types import ToolAnnotations\n\nNothing has changed since 1dfd's decision, so this ticket applies the same path-2 rule:\nland the safe subset, leave mcp pinned <2. 732b remains the home for the migration.\n\nLock-refresh method + fidelity:\n  * pyproject: the single 'zizmor==1.28.0' -> 'zizmor==1.29.0' (exact pin kept exact).\n  * uv.lock regenerated with 'uv lock --upgrade-package zizmor' (not hand-edited).\n    Resulting diff is 30 lines, confined to the zizmor package block; uv.lock 'revision'\n    stays 2 (unchanged from main), and no marker churn was introduced.\n  * All 11 zizmor 1.29.0 hashes (1 sdist + 10 wheels) are BYTE-IDENTICAL to the ones in\n    'gh pr diff 125' — diffed and confirmed, so this reproduces dependabot's intent exactly.\n  * 'uv lock --check' exits 0 (the same gate CI runs at _build-and-test.yml:67).\n  * mcp confirmed still at 1.29.0 in uv.lock and '>=1.28.1,<2' in both pyproject sites.\n\nNote on the PR's other diff noise: dependabot's uv.lock rewrite also bumps the lock\n'revision' 2 -> 3 and adds extra-marker churn across ~20 unrelated packages. That is an\nartifact of the newer uv dependabot runs, not part of either bump; regenerating locally\nreproduces neither, which keeps this change reviewable."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786097316986664001,"uuid":"a14e9c46-7c60-4037-a6cc-3bcdbb5410f6"}